  "reasoning": "The defendants pretended to have a legitimate tourism development project, forged bank documents, and used false statements to induce construction companies to sign contracts and pay deposits, guarantee money, and other fees. Their conduct fits the legal definition of contract fraud (合同诈骗罪), i.e., using false contracts or false statements to obtain property from others. No other distinct offenses (e.g., violent crimes) are evident, and the prosecution’s focus is on fraud in the contract‑signing process.",
